# Reliability & Cross-cutting

## Resilience
- Expect dependency failure. Timeouts, retries (idempotent only), bulkheads, circuit breakers, graceful degradation.
- Backpressure under overload: shed load, queue, or serve stale/cached reads. Fail loud on critical paths.
- Define degraded modes in advance (read-only, delay settlement, disable non-critical features).

## Backup vs rollback
- Backup/PITR is for **data loss**. Rolling back a bad release is **code/flags**. Wrong bookings/payments need **compensation**, not yesterday’s dump — see `backup-rollback.mdc`.

## Disaster recovery
- Written **RPO/RTO** per critical datastore. Automated backups + **restore drills** on a schedule.
- Paying / SLA prod: multi-AZ (or equivalent HA). Tiny internal tools may defer HA — document the risk.
- Multi-region only with clear failover ownership and runbook — never “set and forget”.
- Avoid split-brain; one write source of truth. Document who declares disaster failover.

## Data integrity
- Consistency per use case (strong vs eventual); show stale in UX when eventual.
- See also `concurrency-correctness.mdc` and `messaging-integration.mdc` for races and outbox.

## FinOps
- Budget alerts; right-size; kill idle; efficient queries before bigger machines; unit cost per request/user.

## Compliance & product ops
- Classify data; audit admin and money actions; status page; controlled impersonation; enforce abuse limits in product+infra.
